From df8580c2f19e69cf9abf62b9470e9ed654a40340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:10:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/35] feat(hybrid): kyty_gpu.dll bridge for AnyPS5's native
 AstroBot.exe (milestone 1)

Kyty's GPU stack as a DLL that exports the 82 graphics NIDs AstroBot.exe
imports (65 libSceAgc, 6 libSceAgcDriver, 11 libSceVideoOut). Each export is
a System V-transparent thunk through a slot; init binds the slots through
Kyty's own LIB_FUNC tables, except sceAgcDriverAddEqEvent and
sceVideoOutAddFlipEvent, whose queue handles belong to AnyPS5's libkernel and
go to host callbacks. Versioned C interface in src/hybrid/kytyGpuApi.h.

Built by tools/hybrid/build_kyty_gpu.py from the existing kyty_emulator
objects (bridge compiled with the same flags); tests/hybrid/kytyGpuLoadTest.c,
built with MinGW GCC, passes 351 checks (352 with AnyPS5's winpthread
preloaded). Renderer start-up, memory adapter and event delivery are
milestone 2 and return KYTY_GPU_E_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
